From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Cui <bh@bugs.cc>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:41:58 -0400
Subject: fix: set aside a differing history file instead of dropping the
 profile's copy

`--share-history` first merges the history a session profile accumulated
on its own into `~/.claude`, then links the profile to it. The merge
treats every same-named file as a duplicate: when the target already
exists the profile's copy is unlinked without comparing content
(realiti4/claude-swap#241). That assumption only holds for a transcript
that is byte-identical on both sides. A transcript UUID can exist on both
sides with different content when a session was continued in the profile
after an un-share, and a project's `memory/MEMORY.md` is one fixed name
whose two copies are usually both real. In both cases the profile's copy
vanished silently, and there is no way to tell afterwards what was lost.

The merge now drops the profile's copy only when both files are
byte-identical. A differing copy is moved to
`<backup>/history-conflicts/<profile>/<run>/<item>/<relative path>`: the
shared copy is never overwritten, the profile's copy is never lost, and
the launch names the directory it was parked in. `--purge` mentions the
directory when it exists, since it lives inside the backup dir that purge
removes.

